ue hacer.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-remember-doing"]},{"id":"b2-u01-l03-e03","lesson_id":"b2-u01-l03","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"We were tired, so we stopped ___ a coffee.","translation":"Estábamos cansados, así que paramos para tomar un café.","options":["to have","having","have","had"]},"answer":"to have","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Stop + to: parar para hacer otra cosa. Stop + -ing: dejar de hacerla.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-remember-doing"]},{"id":"b2-u01-l03-e04","lesson_id":"b2-u01-l03","position":4,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"I regret ___ those things to my brother.","translation":"Me arrepiento de haberle dicho esas cosas a mi hermano.","options":["saying","to say","say","said"]},"answer":"saying","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Regret + -ing: te arrepientes de algo que hiciste.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-regret"]},{"id":"b2-u01-l03-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u01-l03","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lee y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u1-apology","document":"email","setting":"Un correo que intenta aclarar un malentendido.","from":"Nina","to":"Mark","title":"About my email","lines":["Hi Mark,","I want to apologize for my email yesterday. I realize it sounded rude, and I regret writing it in such a hurry.","I did not mean to criticize your work. Actually, the report is very good. I only wanted to show you one mistake in the numbers before the meeting.","Next time I will stop to think before I click \"send\". If you have a minute today, I would be happy to talk about it.","Best wishes,","Nina"]},"question":"¿De qué se arrepiente Nina?","options":["De haber escrito el correo con apuro","De haber criticado el informe","De no haber ido a la reunión","De haber llamado a Mark"]},"answer":"De haber escrito el correo con apuro","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Nina escribe: «I regret writing it in such a hurry».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u01-l03-e06","lesson_id":"b2-u01-l03","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lee y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u1-apology","document":"email","setting":"Un correo que intenta aclarar un malentendido.","from":"Nina","to":"Mark","title":"About my email","lines":["Hi Mark,","I want to apologize for my email yesterday. I realize it sounded rude, and I regret writing it in such a hurry.","I did not mean to criticize your work. Actually, the report is very good. I only wanted to show you one mistake in the numbers before the meeting.","Next time I will stop to think before I click \"send\". If you have a minute today, I would be happy to talk about it.","Best wishes,","Nina"]},"question":"¿Qué hará Nina la próxima vez?","options":["Parar a pensar antes de hacer clic en «enviar»","Dejar de mandar correos","Pedirle a Mark que revise sus correos","Escribir más rápido"]},"answer":"Parar a pensar antes de hacer clic en «enviar»","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Nina escribe: «Next time I will stop to think before I click \"send\"» (stop + to = parar para).","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u01-l03-e07","lesson_id":"b2-u01-l03","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y elige lo que oyes","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"I regret saying those things to my brother.","options":["I regret saying those things to my brother.","I regret saying those things to my mother.","I don't regret saying those things to my brother.","I regret not saying those things to my brother."]},"answer":"I regret saying those things to my brother.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-regret"]},{"id":"b2-u01-l03-e08","lesson_id":"b2-u01-l03","position":8,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Ordena las palabras","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["Remember","to","call","your","grandmother","tonight"],"translation":"Acuérdate de llamar a tu abuela esta noche."},"answer":"Remember to call your grandmother tonight.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["en-remember-doing"]},{"id":"b2-u01-l03-e09","lesson_id":"b2-u01-l03","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Responde en inglés","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"Are you still smoking? (dejaste de fumar hace dos años)","translation":"¿Fumas?"},"answer":"No, I stopped smoking two years ago.","accepted_answers":["I stopped smoking two years ago.","No, I stopped two years ago.","No. I stopped smoking two years ago."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-remember-doing"]},{"id":"b2-u01-l03-e10","lesson_id":"b2-u01-l03","position":10,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduce al inglés","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Me acuerdo de haberla conocido, pero me olvidé de preguntarle el nombre."},"answer":"I remember meeting her, but I forgot to ask her name.","accepted_answers":["I remember meeting her but I forgot to ask her name.","I remember meeting her, but I forgot to ask her what her name was."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-remember-doing"]},{"id":"b2-u01-l04-e01","lesson_id":"b2-u01-l04","position":1,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Une cada palabra con su significado","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"straightforward","right":"directo / franco"},{"left":"blunt","right":"brusco / demasiado directo"},{"left":"tactful","right":"con tacto / diplomático"},{"left":"bring up","right":"sacar (un tema) / mencionar"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-straightforward","en-blunt","en-tactful","en-bring-up"]},{"id":"b2-u01-l04-e02","lesson_id":"b2-u01-l04","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"She pointed ___ a mistake in my report.","translation":"Señaló un error en mi informe.","options":["out","up","on","off"]},"answer":"out","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-point-out"]},{"id":"b2-u01-l04-e03","lesson_id":"b2-u01-l04","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Sorry to be ___, but your plan won’t work.","translation":"Perdón por ser tan directo, pero tu plan no va a funcionar.","options":["blunt","tactful","polite","friendly"]},"answer":"blunt","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Blunt: tan directo que puede caer mal. Se usa para disculparse antes de una crítica.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-blunt"]},{"id":"b2-u01-l04-e04","lesson_id":"b2-u01-l04","position":4,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"People ___ speak faster when they are nervous.","translation":"La gente tiende a hablar más rápido cuando está nerviosa.","options":["tend to","seem","mean to","used"]},"answer":"tend to","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-tend-to"]},{"id":"b2-u01-l04-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u01-l04","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lee y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u1-feedback-post","document":"post","setting":"Una publicación de un blog sobre cómo dar una opinión difícil.","title":"How to say difficult things","lines":["Most of us tend to avoid difficult conversations. We are afraid of hurting people, so we say nothing, or we drop a hint and hope the other person understands.","The problem is that hints are easy to miss. Your colleague may not realize there is a problem at all.","Being straightforward does not mean being blunt. Start with something positive, then point out the problem clearly and calmly, and finally look for a solution together.","Remember: people can accept honest feedback when it is tactful. What they find hard to accept is sarcasm."]},"question":"Según el texto, ¿cuál es el problema de las indirectas?","options":["Que es fácil no darse cuenta de ellas","Que son maleducadas","Que llevan mucho tiempo","Que siempre ofenden"]},"answer":"Que es fácil no darse cuenta de ellas","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"El texto dice: «The problem is that hints are easy to miss».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u01-l04-e06","lesson_id":"b2-u01-l04","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lee y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u1-feedback-post","document":"post","setting":"Una publicación de un blog sobre cómo dar una opinión difícil.","title":"How to say difficult things","lines":["Most of us tend to avoid difficult conversations. We are afraid of hurting people, so we say nothing, or we drop a hint and hope the other person understands.","The problem is that hints are easy to miss. Your colleague may not realize there is a problem at all.","Being straightforward does not mean being blunt. Start with something positive, then point out the problem clearly and calmly, and finally look for a solution together.","Remember: people can accept honest feedback when it is tactful. What they find hard to accept is sarcasm."]},"question":"¿Qué diferencia hace el texto entre straightforward y blunt?","options":["Se puede ser claro sin ser brusco","Son lo mismo","Ser brusco funciona mejor","Hay que evitar ser claro"]},"answer":"Se puede ser claro sin ser brusco","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"El texto dice: «Being straightforward does not mean being blunt».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u01-l04-e07","lesson_id":"b2-u01-l04","position":7,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lee y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u1-feedback-post","document":"post","setting":"Una publicación de un blog sobre cómo dar una opinión difícil.","title":"How to say difficult things","lines":["Most of us tend to avoid difficult conversations. We are afraid of hurting people, so we say nothing, or we drop a hint and hope the other person understands.","The problem is that hints are easy to miss. Your colleague may not realize there is a problem at all.","Being straightforward does not mean being blunt. Start with something positive, then point out the problem clearly and calmly, and finally look for a solution together.","Remember: people can accept honest feedback when it is tactful. What they find hard to accept is sarcasm."]},"question":"¿Qué es lo que, según el texto, la gente acepta peor?","options":["El sarcasmo","Una opinión sincera","Un comentario positivo","Una solución en conjunto"]},"answer":"El sarcasmo","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"El texto dice: «people can accept honest feedback when it is tactful. What they find hard to accept is sarcasm».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u01-l04-e08","lesson_id":"b2-u01-l04","position":8,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y elige lo que oyes","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Don't bring up politics at dinner.","options":["Don't bring up politics at dinner.","Don't bring up politics at work.","Do bring up politics at dinner.","Don't talk about politics at dinner."]},"answer":"Don't bring up politics at dinner.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-bring-up"]},{"id":"b2-u01-l04-e09","lesson_id":"b2-u01-l04","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Responde en inglés","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"Should I tell him about the problem? (sí, pero con tacto)","translation":"¿Le cuento del problema?"},"answer":"Yes, but be tactful.","accepted_answers":["Yes, but try to be tactful.","Yes, but you should be tactful.","Yes. But be tactful."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-tactful"]},{"id":"b2-u01-l04-e10","lesson_id":"b2-u01-l04","position":10,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduce al inglés","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Señaló un error en mi informe."},"answer":"She pointed out a mistake in my report.","accepted_answers":["He pointed out a mistake in my report.","She pointed out an error in my report.","He pointed out an error in my report."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-point-out"]},{"id":"b2-u01-rev2-e01","lesson_id":"b2-u01-rev2","position":1,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduce al inglés","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Señaló un error en mi informe."},"answer":"She pointed out a mistake in my report.","accepted_answers":["He pointed out a mistake in my report.","She pointed out an error in my report.","He pointed out an error in my report."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-point-out"]},{"id":"b2-u01-rev2-e02","lesson_id":"b2-u01-rev2","position":2,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Responde en inglés","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"Should I tell him about the problem? (sí, pero con tacto)","translation":"¿Le cuento del problema?"},"answer":"Yes, but be tactful.","accepted_answers":["Yes, but try to be tactful.","Yes, but you should be tactful.","Yes. But be tactful."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-tactful"]},{"id":"b2-u01-rev2-e04","lesson_id":"b2-u01-rev2","position":4,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"I regret ___ those things to my brother.","translation":"Me arrepiento de haberle dicho esas cosas a mi hermano.","options":["saying","to say","say","said"]},"answer":"saying","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Regret + -ing: te arrepientes de algo que hiciste.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-regret"]},{"id":"b2-u01-rev2-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u01-rev2","position":5,"type":"complete_word","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Escribe la palabra completa","payload":{"type":"complete_word","masked":"b_i_g u_","hint":"sacar (un tema) / mencionar"},"answer":"bring up","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":20,"words":["en-bring-up"]},{"id":"b2-u01-rev2-e07","lesson_id":"b2-u01-rev2","position":7,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduce al inglés","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"tender a / soler"},"answer":"tend to","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-tend-to"]},{"id":"b2-u01-rev2-e08","lesson_id":"b2-u01-rev2","position":8,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduce al inglés","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Me acuerdo de haberla conocido, pero me olvidé de preguntarle el nombre."},"answer":"I remember meeting her, but I forgot to ask her name.","accepted_answers":["I remember meeting her but I forgot to ask her name.","I remember meeting her, but I forgot to ask her what her name was."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-remember-doing"]},{"id":"b2-u01-rev2-e09","lesson_id":"b2-u01-rev2","position":9,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y elige lo que oyes","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"blunt","options":["blunt","sarcastic","tone","bring up"]},"answer":"blunt","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-blunt"]},{"id":"b2-u01-rev2-e10","lesson_id":"b2-u01-rev2","position":10,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Une cada palabra con su significado","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"straightforward","right":"directo / franco"},{"left":"blunt","right":"brusco / demasiado directo"},{"left":"bring up","right":"sacar (un tema) / mencionar"},{"left":"tend to","right":"tender a / soler"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-straightforward","en-blunt","en-bring-up","en-tend-to"]},{"id":"b2-u01-l05-e02","lesson_id":"b2-u01-l05","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"His body ___ showed that he was nervous.","translation":"Su lenguaje corporal mostraba que estaba nervioso.","options":["language","tone","eyes","hint"]},"answer":"language","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-body-language"]},{"id":"b2-u01-l05-e03","lesson_id":"b2-u01-l05","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"It is hard to get your ideas ___ in a short message.","translation":"Es difícil transmitir tus ideas en un mensaje corto.","options":["across","out","up","off"]},"answer":"across","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-get-across"]},{"id":"b2-u01-l05-e04","lesson_id":"b2-u01-l05","position":4,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"He ___ to be tired. He keeps closing his eyes.","translation":"Parece estar cansado. No para de cerrar los ojos.","options":["seems","means","tends","implies"]},"answer":"seems","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Seem to + verbo: parecer (por lo que ves).","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-seem"]},{"id":"b2-u01-l05-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u01-l05","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u1-dinner","setting":"Dos amigos comentan una cena de la noche anterior.","speakers":[{"name":"Leo","voice":"a"},{"name":"Ivy","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Leo","text":"Did you notice what Carla said at dinner? \"Some people never offer to pay.\""},{"speaker":"Ivy","text":"I did. Apparently she was talking about Tom. He always forgets his wallet."},{"speaker":"Leo","text":"So she was implying that he never pays? That was a pretty strong hint."},{"speaker":"Ivy","text":"Well, I don't think she meant to embarrass him. She was being sarcastic, but in a friendly way."},{"speaker":"Leo","text":"Tom didn't seem to find it funny, though. He went quiet for the rest of the night."},{"speaker":"Ivy","text":"Maybe I'll bring it up with Carla. She'd want to know he was hurt."}]},"question":"¿Qué piensa hacer Ivy?","options":["Hablar del tema con Carla","Pedirle perdón a Tom","Invitar a Tom a cenar","No meterse"]},"answer":"Hablar del tema con Carla","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Ivy dice: «Maybe I’ll bring it up with Carla. She’d want to know he was hurt».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u01-l05-e06","lesson_id":"b2-u01-l05","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u1-email-tone","setting":"Dos compañeros de trabajo hablan de un correo que cayó mal.","speakers":[{"name":"Nina","voice":"a"},{"name":"Sam","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Nina","text":"Can I ask you something? Did my email this morning seem rude to you?"},{"speaker":"Sam","text":"Honestly? It was a bit short. You just wrote \"Fix this today.\" No hello, no thanks."},{"speaker":"Nina","text":"Oh no. I didn't mean to sound angry. I was in a hurry, that's all."},{"speaker":"Sam","text":"I know, but Mark actually thought you were annoyed with him."},{"speaker":"Nina","text":"That's a misunderstanding. I'll call him and explain."},{"speaker":"Sam","text":"Good idea. A call is better than another email. Tone doesn't always get across in writing."}]},"question":"¿Qué explica Nina sobre su correo?","options":["Que no quiso sonar enojada: estaba apurada","Que estaba enojada con Mark","Que no lo escribió ella","Que lo mandó por error"]},"answer":"Que no quiso sonar enojada: estaba apurada","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Nina dice: «I didn’t mean to sound angry. I was in a hurry, that’s all».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u01-l05-e07","lesson_id":"b2-u01-l05","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y elige lo que oyes","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"His body language showed that he was nervous.","options":["His body language showed that he was nervous.","His body language showed that he was angry.","Her body language showed that she was nervous.","His tone showed that he was nervous."]},"answer":"His body language showed that he was nervous.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-body-language"]},{"id":"b2-u01-l05-e08","lesson_id":"b2-u01-l05","position":8,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Ordena las palabras","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["People","tend","to","look","away","when","they","are"