 que viene.","options":["to be","being","be","will be"]},"answer":"to be","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Be expected + to + verbo.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-be-expected-to"]},{"id":"b2-u03-l03-e03","lesson_id":"b2-u03-l03","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"It is a ___ idea, but it is not true.","translation":"Es una idea muy extendida, pero no es cierta.","options":["widespread","average","local","lonely"]},"answer":"widespread","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-widespread"]},{"id":"b2-u03-l03-e04","lesson_id":"b2-u03-l03","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u3-podcast","setting":"Un pódcast entrevista a una socióloga sobre las generaciones.","speakers":[{"name":"Host","voice":"a"},{"name":"Dr. Reyes","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"People often complain that young people have no respect for old customs. Is that true?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Every generation has said that about the next one. It is said that even the ancient Greeks complained about their teenagers."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"So nothing has really changed?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Customs change, of course. Fewer people get married in church, for example, and family dinners are less common. But the values behind them haven't disappeared."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"What do you mean?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Young people still care about their families. They just show it in different ways: a video call instead of a Sunday lunch."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And is the gap between generations getting bigger?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Honestly, I don't think so. Many people believe that, but my research shows that parents and children agree about most things."}]},"question":"¿Para qué menciona la socióloga a los antiguos griegos?","options":["Para mostrar que la queja sobre los jóvenes es muy antigua","Para hablar de la historia de Grecia","Para decir que los griegos eran mejores","Para explicar una costumbre griega"]},"answer":"Para mostrar que la queja sobre los jóvenes es muy antigua","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Dice: «It is said that even the ancient Greeks complained about their teenagers».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u03-l03-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u03-l03","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u3-podcast","setting":"Un pódcast entrevista a una socióloga sobre las generaciones.","speakers":[{"name":"Host","voice":"a"},{"name":"Dr. Reyes","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"People often complain that young people have no respect for old customs. Is that true?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Every generation has said that about the next one. It is said that even the ancient Greeks complained about their teenagers."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"So nothing has really changed?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Customs change, of course. Fewer people get married in church, for example, and family dinners are less common. But the values behind them haven't disappeared."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"What do you mean?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Young people still care about their families. They just show it in different ways: a video call instead of a Sunday lunch."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And is the gap between generations getting bigger?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Honestly, I don't think so. Many people believe that, but my research shows that parents and children agree about most things."}]},"question":"¿Qué opina la socióloga de la idea de que la distancia entre generaciones es cada vez mayor?","options":["Que mucha gente lo cree, pero su investigación no lo confirma","Que es cierta","Que es nueva","Que nadie la cree"]},"answer":"Que mucha gente lo cree, pero su investigación no lo confirma","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Dice: «Many people believe that, but my research shows that parents and children agree about most things».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u03-l03-e06","lesson_id":"b2-u03-l03","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lee y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u3-market","document":"notice","setting":"Un aviso de la municipalidad sobre el mercado viejo.","title":"Our market is changing","lines":["The old market is being renovated and will be closed until the end of May.","The roof has already been repaired, and new lights are being installed this month.","The market has been used by local families for more than a hundred years. It is believed to be the oldest building in the neighborhood.","When the work is finished, the market will be used for concerts and festivals. The first festival is expected to take place in June.","Questions can be sent to the community office."]},"question":"¿Qué se cree del mercado?","options":["Que es el edificio más viejo del barrio","Que va a cerrar para siempre","Que es el más grande de la ciudad","Que lo construyó una familia"]},"answer":"Que es el edificio más viejo del barrio","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"El aviso dice: «It is believed to be the oldest building in the neighborhood».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u03-l03-e07","lesson_id":"b2-u03-l03","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y elige lo que oyes","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"It is said that the house is two hundred years old.","options":["It is said that the house is two hundred years old.","It is said that the house is three hundred years old.","It was said that the house was two hundred years old.","They say that the house is two hundred years old."]},"answer":"It is said that the house is two hundred years old.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-it-is-said"]},{"id":"b2-u03-l03-e08","lesson_id":"b2-u03-l03","position":8,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Ordena las palabras","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["The","festival","is","expected","to","take","place","in","June"],"translation":"Se espera que el festival se realice en junio."},"answer":"The festival is expected to take place in June.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["en-be-expected-to","en-take-place"]},{"id":"b2-u03-l03-e09","lesson_id":"b2-u03-l03","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Responde en inglés","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"When will the homes be ready? (se espera que estén listas el año que viene)","translation":"¿Cuándo van a estar listas las viviendas?"},"answer":"They are expected to be ready next year.","accepted_answers":["They're expected to be ready next year.","They are expected to be finished next year.","Next year, they are expected to be ready."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-be-expected-to"]},{"id":"b2-u03-l03-e10","lesson_id":"b2-u03-l03","position":10,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduce al inglés","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Se dice que la casa tiene doscientos años."},"answer":"It is said that the house is two hundred years old.","accepted_answers":["It's said that the house is two hundred years old.","It is said the house is two hundred years old.","The house is said to be two hundred years old."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-it-is-said"]},{"id":"b2-u03-l04-e01","lesson_id":"b2-u03-l04","position":1,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Une cada palabra con su significado","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"housing","right":"vivienda"},{"left":"take place","right":"tener lugar / realizarse"},{"left":"is being built","right":"se está construyendo"},{"left":"widespread","right":"generalizado / extendido"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-housing","en-take-place","en-being-built","en-widespread"]},{"id":"b2-u03-l04-e02","lesson_id":"b2-u03-l04","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"A new school is ___ built near my house.","translation":"Se está construyendo una escuela nueva cerca de mi casa.","options":["being","been","be","was"]},"answer":"being","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Pasiva continua: is / are + being + participio.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-being-built"]},{"id":"b2-u03-l04-e03","lesson_id":"b2-u03-l04","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"The roof has already ___ repaired.","translation":"El techo ya fue reparado.","options":["been","being","be","was"]},"answer":"been","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Pasiva en present perfect: has / have + been + participio.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-being-built"]},{"id":"b2-u03-l04-e04","lesson_id":"b2-u03-l04","position":4,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"The festival will take ___ in the old market.","translation":"El festival se va a realizar en el mercado viejo.","options":["place","part","time","care"]},"answer":"place","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-take-place"]},{"id":"b2-u03-l04-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u03-l04","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u3-radio","setting":"Un informe en la radio sobre el último censo de una ciudad.","speakers":[{"name":"Presenter","voice":"a"},{"name":"Anna","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"Good morning. The results of the new census have just been published. Anna, what do they tell us?"},{"speaker":"Anna","text":"The population of the city has risen by ten percent in five years, mainly because of young people from other regions."},{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"And where are they living?"},{"speaker":"Anna","text":"That's the problem. Housing is very expensive, so the average young person shares a flat until the age of thirty."},{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"Is anything being done about it?"},{"speaker":"Anna","text":"Two thousand new homes are being built near the river, and more are expected to be ready next year."},{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"Thank you, Anna. In other news, the summer festival will take place in the old market this year."}]},"question":"¿Por qué los jóvenes comparten apartamento hasta los treinta, según el informe?","options":["Porque la vivienda es muy cara","Porque no consiguen trabajo","Porque prefieren vivir con amigos","Porque estudian hasta los treinta"]},"answer":"Porque la vivienda es muy cara","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Anna dice: «Housing is very expensive, so the average young person shares a flat until the age of thirty».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u03-l04-e06","lesson_id":"b2-u03-l04","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u3-radio","setting":"Un informe en la radio sobre el último censo de una c