[]},{"id":"b2-u06-l03-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u06-l03","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lee y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u6-advice","document":"post","setting":"Una columna de consejos: la carta de una lectora y la respuesta.","title":"Ask Ruth","lines":["Dear Ruth, Last week I fell out with my best friend. She was an hour late for my birthday dinner, and I shouted at her in front of everyone. Now I feel guilty, but I am also still a bit angry. What should I do? — Lina","Dear Lina, It sounds like you both made mistakes. Being an hour late is rude, and you had every right to be upset. However, you probably overreacted when you shouted at her in public.","Try not to take it personally. She could have had a good reason for being late. Call her, tell her how you felt, and listen to her side of the story.","Friends fall out all the time. What matters is how you make up. — Ruth"]},"question":"¿Cuál es la opinión de Ruth?","options":["Las dos se equivocaron: llegar tarde fue grosero, pero Lina exageró","Sólo se equivocó la amiga","Sólo se equivocó Lina","Ninguna se equivocó"]},"answer":"Las dos se equivocaron: llegar tarde fue grosero, pero Lina exageró","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Ruth responde: «you both made mistakes… you probably overreacted when you shouted at her in public».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u06-l03-e06","lesson_id":"b2-u06-l03","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lee y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u6-advice","document":"post","setting":"Una columna de consejos: la carta de una lectora y la respuesta.","title":"Ask Ruth","lines":["Dear Ruth, Last week I fell out with my best friend. She was an hour late for my birthday dinner, and I shouted at her in front of everyone. Now I feel guilty, but I am also still a bit angry. Wha