esando mucho con tu inglés.","options":["making","doing","having","taking"]},"answer":"making","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Collocation: make progress (no «do progress»).","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-make-progress"]},{"id":"b2-u09-l03-e03","lesson_id":"b2-u09-l03","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Good teachers help students reach their ___.","translation":"Los buenos profesores ayudan a los alumnos a desarrollar su potencial.","options":["potential","mindset","motivation","talent"]},"answer":"potential","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-potential"]},{"id":"b2-u09-l03-e04","lesson_id":"b2-u09-l03","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lee y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u9-mindset","document":"post","setting":"Un artículo de divulgación sobre la mentalidad de crecimiento.","title":"It is not about talent","lines":["Why do some students give up after one bad grade, while others work harder? According to many psychologists, the answer is their mindset.","People with a \"fixed mindset\" believe that intelligence is something you are born with. When they struggle, they think: \"I am just not good at this.\"","People with a \"growth mindset\" believe that ability can be developed. For them, a mistake is not a failure but information: it shows what to practice next.","The good news is that mindset can change. Teachers who praise effort instead of talent help students reach their potential, and students who see their progress stay motivated for longer."]},"question":"¿Qué piensan las personas con «mentalidad fija» cuando algo les cuesta?","options":["Que simplemente no son buenas para eso","Que tienen que practicar más","Que el profesor es malo","Que es cuestión de tiempo"]},"answer":"Que simplemente no son buenas para eso","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"El artículo dice: «When they struggle, they think: \"I am just not good at this.\"».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u09-l03-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u09-l03","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lee y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u9-mindset","document":"post","setting":"Un artículo de divulgación sobre la mentalidad de crecimiento.","title":"It is not about talent","lines":["Why do some students give up after one bad grade, while others work harder? According to many psychologists, the answer is their mindset.","People with a \"fixed mindset\" believe that intelligence is something you are born with. When they struggle, they think: \"I am just not good at this.\"","People with a \"growth mindset\" believe that ability can be developed. For them, a mistake is not a failure but information: it shows what to practice next.","The good news is that mindset can change. Teachers who praise effort instead of talent help students reach their potential, and students who see their progress stay motivated for longer."]},"question":"Para quien tiene «mentalidad de crecimiento», ¿qué es un error?","options":["Información que muestra qué practicar después","Un fracaso","Una razón para abandonar","Algo que hay que ocultar"]},"answer":"Información que muestra qué practicar después","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"El artículo dice: «a mistake is not a failure but information: it shows what to practice next».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u09-l03-e06","lesson_id":"b2-u09-l03","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lee y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u9-mindset","document":"post","setting":"Un artículo de divulgación sobre la mentalidad de crecimiento.","title":"It is not about talent","lines":["Why do some students give up after one bad grade, while others work harder? According to many psychologists, the answer is their mindset.","People with a \"fixed mindset\" believe that intelligence is something you are born with. When they struggle, they think: \"I am just not good at this.\"","People with a \"growth mindset\" believe that ability can be developed. For them, a mistake is not a failure but information: it shows what to practice next.","The good news is that mindset can change. Teachers who praise effort instead of talent help students reach their potential, and students who see their progress stay motivated for longer."]},"question":"¿Qué ayuda a que los alumnos sigan motivados más tiempo?","options":["Ver su propio progreso","Sacar buenas notas","Tener talento","Estudiar solos"]},"answer":"Ver su propio progreso","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"El artículo dice: «students who see their progress stay motivated for longer».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u09-l03-e07","lesson_id":"b2-u09-l03","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y elige lo que oyes","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Motivation comes and goes.","options":["Motivation comes and goes.","Motivation comes and stays.","Motivation goes and comes back.","Money comes and goes."]},"answer":"Motivation comes and goes.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-motivation"]},{"id":"b2-u09-l03-e08","lesson_id":"b2-u09-l03","position":8,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Ordena las palabras","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["Your","mindset","is","more","important","than","your","talent"],"translation":"Tu forma de pensar es más importante que tu talento."},"answer":"Your mindset is more important than your talent.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["en-mindset"]},{"id":"b2-u09-l03-e09","lesson_id":"b2-u09-l03","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Responde en inglés","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"How is your English going? (estás progresando mucho)","translation":"¿Cómo va tu inglés?"},"answer":"I am making great progress.","accepted_answers":["I'm making great progress.","I'm making a lot of progress.","I am making good progress."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-make-progress"]},{"id":"b2-u09-l03-e10","lesson_id":"b2-u09-l03","position":10,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduce al inglés","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"La motivación va y viene."},"answer":"Motivation comes and goes.","accepted_answers":["Motivation comes and goes!"],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-motivation"]},{"id":"b2-u09-l04-e01","lesson_id":"b2-u09-l04","position":1,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Une cada palabra con su significado","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"procrastinate","right":"postergar / dejar para después"},{"left":"self-discipline","right":"autodisciplina / constancia"},{"left":"keep track of","right":"llevar la cuenta de / registrar"},{"left":"catch up","right":"ponerse al día"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-procrastinate","en-self-discipline","en-keep-track-of","en-catch-up"]},{"id":"b2-u09-l04-e02","lesson_id":"b2-u09-l04","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"I keep ___ of my study hours in a notebook.","translation":"Llevo la cuenta de mis horas de estudio en un cuaderno.","options":["track","list","time","care"]},"answer":"track","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-keep-track-of"]},{"id":"b2-u09-l04-e03","lesson_id":"b2-u09-l04","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"I missed two classes, so I need to catch ___.","translation":"Falté a dos clases, así que tengo que ponerme al día.","options":["up","on","out","off"]},"answer":"up","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-catch-up"]},{"id":"b2-u09-l04-e04","lesson_id":"b2-u09-l04","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lee y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u9-procrastinate","document":"post","setting":"Una publicación de blog sobre dejar de postergar.","title":"How I stopped putting things off","lines":["For years I was an expert at procrastinating. I cleaned my room, checked my phone, made coffee… anything except studying.","What finally helped was not motivation. Motivation comes and goes. What I needed was self-discipline: a routine that works even on bad days.","Now I study for twenty-five minutes, then take a five-minute break. I keep track of every session in a notebook, and seeing the list grow is surprisingly satisfying.","If you have never tried it, give it a try. It feels strange at first, a bit outside your comfort zone, but after two weeks it becomes a habit."]},"question":"Según el autor, ¿qué lo ayudó a dejar de postergar?","options":["La autodisciplina: una rutina que funciona aun en los días malos","La motivación","Un profesor particular","Apagar el teléfono"]},"answer":"La autodisciplina: una rutina que funciona aun en los días malos","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Escribe: «What finally helped was not motivation… What I needed was self-discipline: a routine that works even on bad days».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u09-l04-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u09-l04","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lee y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u9-procrastinate","document":"post","setting":"Una publicación de blog sobre dejar de postergar.","title":"How I stopped putting things off","lines":["For years I was an expert at procrastinating. I cleaned my room, checked my phone, made coffee… anything except studying.","What finally helped was not motivation. Motivation comes and goes. What I needed was self-discipline: a routine that works even on bad days.","Now I study for twenty-five minutes, then take a five-minute break. I keep track of every session in a notebook, and seeing the list grow is surprisingly satisfying.","If you have never tried it, give it a try. It feels strange at first, a bit outside your comfort zone, but after two weeks it becomes a habit."]},"question":"¿Qué hace con cada sesión de estudio?","options":["La anota en un cuaderno y le gusta ver crecer la lista","La graba en video","La comparte en las redes","Se la muestra a un amigo"]},"answer":"La anota en un cuaderno y le gusta ver crecer la lista","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Escribe: «I keep track of every session in a notebook, and seeing the list grow is surprisingly satisfying».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u09-l04-e06","lesson_id":"b2-u09-l04","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u9-advisor","setting":"Un estudiante habla con una tutora de la universidad.","speakers":[{"name":"Ivan","voice":"a"},{"name":"Ms. Ortiz","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Ivan","text":"I'm thinking of dropping out. I've missed six weeks of classes because of my job, and I'll never catch up."},{"speaker":"Ms. Ortiz","text":"Wait. Before you decide, have you heard about our scholarship for working students?"},{"speaker":"Ivan","