"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-moreover"]},{"id":"b2-u10-l01-e03","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l01","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"It rained all week. As a ___, the match was canceled.","translation":"Llovió toda la semana. Como resultado, se canceló el partido.","options":["result","reason","end","point"]},"answer":"result","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-as-a-result"]},{"id":"b2-u10-l01-e04","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l01","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u10-school-debate","setting":"Un debate en un colegio: ¿hay que prohibir los teléfonos en clase?","speakers":[{"name":"Moderator","voice":"a"},{"name":"Lucas","voice":"b"},{"name":"Hannah","voice":"a"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Moderator","text":"Today's debate: should phones be banned in schools? Lucas, you're first."},{"speaker":"Lucas","text":"Yes, they should. Phones distract students. Moreover, they make bullying easier, because it continues after school. As a result, many students feel anxious all day."},{"speaker":"Moderator","text":"Hannah, your answer?"},{"speaker":"Hannah","text":"Admittedly, phones can be a distraction. Nevertheless, banning them is not the answer. On the contrary, schools should teach students how to use them responsibly."},{"speaker":"Lucas","text":"But that's an assumption. Where is the evidence that teaching works better?"},{"speaker":"Hannah","text":"Fair question. What I'm saying is that a ban doesn't teach anything. In other words, students will just use their phones more at home."}]},"question":"¿Qué razones da Lucas para prohibir los teléfonos?","options":["Distraen y facilitan el acoso, que sigue después del colegio","Son caros","Se rompen fácilmente","Los profesores no saben usarlos"]},"answer":"Distraen y facilitan el acoso, que sigue después del colegio","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Lucas dice: «Phones distract students. Moreover, they make bullying easier, because it continues after school».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u10-l01-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l01","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u10-school-debate","setting":"Un debate en un colegio: ¿hay que prohibir los teléfonos en clase?","speakers":[{"name":"Moderator","voice":"a"},{"name":"Lucas","voice":"b"},{"name":"Hannah","voice":"a"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Moderator","text":"Today's debate: should phones be banned in schools? Lucas, you're first."},{"speaker":"Lucas","text":"Yes, they should. Phones distract students. Moreover, they make bullying easier, because it continues after school. As a result, many students feel anxious all day."},{"speaker":"Moderator","text":"Hannah, your answer?"},{"speaker":"Hannah","text":"Admittedly, phones can be a distraction. Nevertheless, banning them is not the answer. On the contrary, schools should teach students how to use them responsibly."},{"speaker":"Lucas","text":"But that's an assumption. Where is the evidence that teaching works better?"},{"speaker":"Hannah","text":"Fair question. What I'm saying is that a ban doesn't teach anything. In other words, students will just use their phones more at home."}]},"question":"¿Qué consecuencia menciona Lucas?","options":["Muchos estudiantes se sienten ansiosos todo el día","Los estudiantes sacan malas notas","Los padres se quejan","El colegio gasta más"]},"answer":"Muchos estudiantes se sienten ansiosos todo el día","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Lucas dice: «As a result, many students feel anxious all day».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u10-l01-e06","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l01","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lee y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u10-free-uni","document":"post","setting":"Un artículo de opinión sobre la universidad gratuita.","title":"Education is an investment, not a cost","lines":["Should university be free? I believe it should.","First, education benefits everyone, not only the student. Educated citizens earn more, pay more taxes and are healthier. Furthermore, free education gives poor students the same chances as rich ones.","Admittedly, free universities cost the government a lot of money, and some people argue that students should pay for their own future. Nevertheless, the long-term benefits outweigh the costs.","It is not the cost of education that should worry us, but the cost of ignorance.","To sum up, free university is not a gift. It is an investment in all of us."]},"question":"¿Qué segundo argumento suma la autora con furthermore?","options":["Que la educación gratuita da a los estudiantes pobres las mismas oportunidades","Que los graduados pagan menos impuestos","Que las universidades son baratas","Que los ricos no deberían estudiar"]},"answer":"Que la educación gratuita da a los estudiantes pobres las mismas oportunidades","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"El artículo dice: «Furthermore, free education gives poor students the same chances as rich ones».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u10-l01-e07","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l01","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y elige lo que oyes","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"We had a debate about social media.","options":["We had a debate about social media.","We had a debate about the news.","We have a debate about social media.","They had a debate about social media."]},"answer":"We had a debate about social media.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-debate"]},{"id":"b2-u10-l01-e08","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l01","position":8,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Ordena las palabras","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["Furthermore","free","education","gives","everyone","the","same","chances"],"translation":"Asimismo, la educación gratuita da a todos las mismas oportunidades."},"answer":"Furthermore free education gives everyone the same chances.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["en-furthermore"]},{"id":"b2-u10-l01-e09","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l01","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Responde en inglés","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"The match was canceled. Why? (llovió toda la semana; como resultado, se canceló)","translation":"Se canceló el partido. ¿Por qué?"},"answer":"It rained all week. As a result, it was canceled.","accepted_answers":["It rained all week. As a result, the match was canceled.","It rained all week and as a result it was canceled.","It rained all week, as a result it was canceled."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-as-a-result"]},{"id":"b2-u10-l01-e10","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l01","position":10,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduce al inglés","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"El plan es barato. Además, es fácil de empezar."},"answer":"The plan is cheap. Moreover, it is easy to start.","accepted_answers":["The plan is cheap. Moreover, it's easy to start.","The plan is cheap. Furthermore, it is easy to start.","The plan is cheap. Moreover it is easy to start."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-moreover"]},{"id":"b2-u10-l02-e01","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l02","position":1,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"___ matters is that you tried.","translation":"Lo que importa es que lo intentaste.","options":["What","That","Which","It"]},"answer":"What","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"What… is: «lo que… es». No se dice «That matters is».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-what-matters-is"]},{"id":"b2-u10-l02-e02","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l02","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"The reason ___ I called is that I need your help.","translation":"La razón por la que llamé es que necesito tu ayuda.","options":["why","because","what","for"]},"answer":"why","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"The reason why… is that… (no «is because» en un registro cuidado).","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-the-reason-why"]},{"id":"b2-u10-l02-e03","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l02","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"He was late again. In other ___, he does not care.","translation":"Llegó tarde otra vez. En otras palabras, no le importa.","options":["words","ways","reasons","times"]},"answer":"words","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-in-other-words"]},{"id":"b2-u10-l02-e04","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l02","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u10-four-days","setting":"Unos colegas discuten la propuesta de trabajar cuatro días por semana.","speakers":[{"name":"Olivia","voice":"a"},{"name":"Ken","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"So, the four-day week. What worries me is the customers. Who answers the phone on Fridays?"},{"speaker":"Ken","text":"We'd take turns. The reason why other companies have done it is that people work better when they're rested."},{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"That may be true for some jobs. But we need to take into account that our clients expect us every day."},{"speaker":"Ken","text":"That's a valid point. So let's try it for three months and measure the results."},{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"OK, I find that convincing. All things considered, a trial is a good compromise."}]},"question":"¿Qué le preocupa a Olivia de la semana de cuatro días?","options":["Quién va a atender a los clientes los viernes","Ganar menos","Trabajar más horas","Que Ken no esté"]},"answer":"Quién va a atender a los clientes los viernes","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Olivia dice: «What worries me is the customers. Who answers the phone on Fridays?».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u10-l02-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l02","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u10-four-days","setting":"Unos colegas discuten la propuesta de trabajar cuatro días por semana.","speakers":[{"name":"Olivia","voice":"a"},{"name":"Ken","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"So, the four-day week. What worries me is the customers. Who answers the phone on Fridays?"},{"speaker":"Ken","text":"We'd take turns. The reason why other companies have done it is that people work better when they're rested."},{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"That may be true for some jobs. But we need to take into account that our clients expect us every day."},{"speaker":"Ken","text":"That's a valid point. So let's try it for three months and measure the results."},{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"OK, I find that convincing. All things considered, a trial is a good compromise."}]},"question":"Según Ken, ¿por qué otras empresas adoptaron la semana de cuatro días?","options":["Porque la gente trabaja mejor cuando está descansada","Porque ahorran dinero","Porque los clientes lo pidieron","Porque es la ley"]},"answer":"Porque la gente trabaja mejor cuando está descansada","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Ken dice: «The reason why other companies have done it is that people work better when they’re rested».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u10-l02-e06","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l02","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u10-school-debate","setting":"Un debate en un colegio: ¿hay que prohibir los teléfonos en clase?","speakers":[{"name":"Moderator","voice":"a"},{"name":"Lucas","voice":"b"},{"name":"Hannah","voice":"a"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Moderator","text":"Today's debate: should phones be banned in schools? Lucas, you're first."},{"speaker":"Lucas","text":"Yes, they should. Phones distract students. Moreover, they make bullying easier, because it continues after school. As a result, many students feel anxious all day."},{"speaker":"Moderator","text":"Hannah, your answer?"},{"speaker":"Hannah","text":"Admittedly, phones can be a distraction. Nevertheless, banning them is not the answer. On the contrary, schools should teach students how to use them responsibly."},{"speaker":"Lucas","text":"But that's an assumption. Where is the evidence that teaching works better?"},{"speaker":"Hannah","text":"Fair question. What I'm saying is that a ban doesn't teach anything. In other words, students will just use their phones more at home."}]},"question":"¿Qué aclara Hannah con «In other words…»?","options":["Que con la prohibición los estudiantes sólo van a usar más el teléfono en casa","Que los teléfonos son peligrosos","Que está de acuerdo con Lucas","Que no tiene pruebas"]},"answer":"Que con la prohibición los estudiantes sólo van a usar más el teléfono en casa","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Hannah dice: «a ban doesn’t teach anything. In other words, students will just use their phones more at home».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u10-l02-e07","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l02","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y elige lo que oyes","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"What matters is that you tried.","options":["What matters is that you tried.","What matters is that you won.","It doesn't matter that you tried.","What matters is that we tried."]},"answer":"What matters is that you tried.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-what-matters-is"]},{"id":"b2-u10-l02-e08","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l02","position":8,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Ordena las palabras","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["What","worries","me","is","the","cost"],"translation":"Lo que me preocupa es el costo."},"answer":"What worries me is the cost.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["en-what-matters-is"]},{"id":"b2-u10-l02-e09","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l02","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Responde en inglés","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"Why are you studying English? (la razón es que quieres trabajar en el exterior)","translation":"¿Por qué estudias inglés?"},"answer":"The reason why I am studying English is that I want to work abroad.","accepted_answers":["The reason why I'm studying English is that I want to work abroad.","The reason is that I want to work abroad.","The reason why is that I want to work abroad."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-the-reason-why"]},{"id":"b2-u10-l02-e10","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l02","position":10,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduce al inglés","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Lo que importa es que lo intentaste."},"answer":"What matters is that you tried.","accepted_answers":["What matters is you tried.","What matters is that you tried it."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-what-matters-is"]},{"id":"b2-u10-rev1-e02","lesson_id":"b2-u10-rev1","position":2,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Responde en inglés","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"The match was canceled. Why? (llovió toda la semana; como resultado, se canceló)","translation":"Se canceló el partido. ¿Por qué?"},"answer":"It rained all week. As a result, it was canceled.","accepted_answers":["It rained all week. As a result, the match was canceled.","It rained all week and as a result it was canceled.","It rained all week, as a result it was canceled."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-as-a-result"]},{"id":"b2-u10-rev1-e03","lesson_id":"b2-u10-rev1","position":3,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduce al inglés","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"lo que importa es"},"answer":"what matters is","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-what-matters-is"]},{"id":"b2-u10-rev1-e04","lesson_id":"b2-u10-rev1","position":4,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduce al inglés","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Lo que importa es que lo intentaste."},"answer":"What matters is that you tried.","accepted_answers":["What matters is you tried.","What matters is that you tried it."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-what-matters-is"]},{"id":"b2-u10-rev1-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u10-rev1","position":5,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"___ matters is that you tried.","translation":"Lo que importa es que lo intentaste.","options":["What","That","Which","It"]},"answer":"What","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"What… is: «lo que… es». No se dice «That matters is».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-what-matters-is"]},{"id":"b2-u10-rev1-e06","lesson_id":"b2-u10-rev1","position":6,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduce al inglés","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"El plan es barato. Además, es fácil de empezar."},"answer":"The plan is cheap. Moreover, it is easy to start.","accepted_answers":["The plan is cheap. Moreover, it's easy to start.","The plan is cheap. Furthermore, it is easy to start.","The plan is cheap. Moreover it is easy to start."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-moreover"]},{"id":"b2-u10-rev1-e07","lesson_id":"b2-u10-rev1","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y elige lo que oyes","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"moreover","options":["moreover","as a result","on the contrary","what matters is"]},"answer":"moreover","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-moreover"]},{"id":"b2-u10-rev1-e09","lesson_id":"b2-u10-rev1","position":9,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Une cada palabra con su significado","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"furthermore","right":"asimismo / es más"},{"left":"moreover","right":"además (formal)"},{"left":"in other words","right":"en otras palabras / es decir"},{"left":"what matters is","right":"lo que importa es"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-furthermore","en-moreover","en-in-other-words","en-what-matters-is"]},{"id":"b2-u10-rev1-e10","lesson_id":"b2-u10-rev1","position":10,"type":"complete_word","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Escribe la palabra completa","payload":{"type":"complete_word","masked":"i_ o_h_r w_r_s","hint":"en otras palabras / es decir"},"answer":"in other words","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":20,"words":["en-in-other-words"]},{"id":"b2-u10-l03-e01","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l03","position":1,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Une cada palabra con su significado","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"admittedly","right":"es cierto que / hay que reconocer que"},{"left":"nevertheless","right":"aun así / de todos modos"},{"left":"on the contrary","right":"al contrario"},{"left":"point of view","right":"punto de vista"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-admittedly","en-nevertheless","en-on-the-contrary","en-point-of-view"]},{"id":"b2-u10-l03-e02","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l03","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"It was difficult. ___, we finished on time.","translation":"Fue difícil. Aun así, terminamos a tiempo.","options":["Nevertheless","Moreover","Furthermore","As a result"]},"answer":"Nevertheless","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Nevertheless introduce algo que pasa a pesar de lo anterior.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-nevertheless"]},{"id":"b2-u10-l03-e03","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l03","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"I'm not tired. On the ___, I feel great.","translation":"No estoy cansado. Al contrario, me siento genial.","options":["contrary","other","opposite","way"]},"answer":"contrary","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"On the contrary niega lo anterior. On the other hand agrega otro lado de la misma idea.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-on-the-contrary"]},{"id":"b2-u10-l03-e04","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l03","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u10-school-debate","setting":"Un debate en un colegio: ¿hay que prohibir los teléfonos en clase?","speakers":[{"name":"Moderator","voice":"a"},{"name":"Lucas","voice":"b"},{"name":"Hannah","voice":"a"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Moderator","text":"Today's debate: should phones be banned in schools? Lucas, you're first."},{"speaker":"Lucas","text":"Yes, they should. Phones distract students. Moreover, they make bullying easier, because it continues after school. As a result, many students feel anxious all day."},{"speaker":"Moderator","text":"Hannah, your answer?"},{"speaker":"Hannah","text":"Admittedly, phones can be a distraction. Nevertheless, banning them is not the answer. On the contrary, schools should teach students how to use them responsibly."},{"speaker":"Lucas","text":"But that's an assumption. Where is the evidence that teaching works better?"},{"speaker":"Hannah","text":"Fair question. What I'm saying is that a ban doesn't teach anything. In other words, students will just use their phones more at home."}]},"question":"¿Qué concede Hannah y qué propone en cambio?","options":["Reconoce que los teléfonos distraen, pero propone enseñar a usarlos bien","Acepta prohibirlos","Dice que no distraen","Propone prohibirlos sólo en los exámenes"]},"answer":"Reconoce que los teléfonos distraen, pero propone enseñar a usarlos bien","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Hannah dice: «Admittedly, phones can be a distraction. Nevertheless, banning them is not the answer. On the contrary, schools should teach students how to use them responsibly».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u10-l03-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l03","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lee y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u10-free-uni","document":"post","setting":"Un artículo de opinión sobre la universidad gratuita.","title":"Education is an investment, not a cost","lines":["Should university be free? I believe it should.","First, education benefits everyone, not only the student. Educated citizens earn more, pay more taxes and are healthier. Furthermore, free education gives poor students the same chances as rich ones.","Admittedly, free universities cost the government a lot of money, and some people argue that students should pay for their own future. Nevertheless, the long-term benefits outweigh the costs.","It is not the cost of education that should worry us, but the cost of ignorance.","To sum up, free university is not a gift. It is an investment in all of us."]},"question":"¿Qué reconoce la autora y cómo lo rebate?","options":["Que cuesta mucho al gobierno, pero los beneficios a largo plazo son mayores","Que es injusto, pero necesario","Que los alumnos no lo valoran","Que es imposible, pero hay que intentarlo"]},"answer":"Que cuesta mucho al gobierno, pero los beneficios a largo plazo son mayores","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"El artículo dice: «Admittedly, free universities cost the government a lot of money… Nevertheless, the long-term benefits outweigh the costs».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u10-l03-e06","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l03","position":6,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y elige lo que oyes","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"I understand your point of view, but I disagree.","options":["I understand your point of view, but I disagree.","I understand your point of view, and I agree.","I don't understand your point of view, but I agree.","I understand your idea, but I disagree."]},"answer":"I understand your point of view, but I disagree.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-point-of-view"]},{"id":"b2-u10-l03-e07","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l03","position":7,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Ordena las palabras","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["Admittedly","it","is","expensive","but","it","is","worth","it"],"translation":"Es cierto que es caro, pero vale la pena."},"answer":"Admittedly it is expensive but it is worth it.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["en-admittedly"]},{"id":"b2-u10-l03-e08","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l03","position":8,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Responde en inglés","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"You don't agree with me, do you? (entiendes su punto de vista, pero no estás de acuerdo)","translation":"No estás de acuerdo conmigo, ¿no?"},"answer":"I understand your point of view, but I disagree.","accepted_answers":["I understand your point of view, but I don't agree.","I understand your point of view but I disagree.","No. I understand your point of view, but I don't agree."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-point-of-view"]},{"id":"b2-u10-l03-e09","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l03","position":9,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduce al inglés","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Fue difícil. Aun así, terminamos a tiempo."},"answer":"It was difficult. Nevertheless, we finished on time.","accepted_answers":["It was hard. Nevertheless, we finished on time.","It was difficult. Nevertheless we finished on time."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-nevertheless"]},{"id":"b2-u10-l04-e01","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l04","position":1,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Une cada palabra con su significado","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"valid","right":"válido"},{"left":"convincing","right":"convincente"},{"left":"assumption","right":"suposición / supuesto"},{"left":"take into account","right":"tener en cuenta"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-valid","en-convincing","en-assumption","en-take-into-account"]},{"id":"b2-u10-l04-e02","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l04","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"We need to take the costs ___ account.","translation":"Tenemos que tener en cuenta los costos.","options":["into","in","on","to"]},"answer":"into","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-take-into-account"]},{"id":"b2-u10-l04-e03","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l04","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"That's just an ___. Where is the evidence?","translation":"Eso es sólo una suposición. ¿Dónde están las pruebas?","options":["assumption","argument","opinion","answer"]},"answer":"assumption","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-assumption"]},{"id":"b2-u10-l04-e04","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l04","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u10-school-debate","setting":"Un debate en un colegio: ¿hay que prohibir los teléfonos en clase?","speakers":[{"name":"Moderator","voice":"a"},{"name":"Lucas","voice":"b"},{"name":"Hannah","voice":"a"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Moderator","text":"Today's debate: should phones be banned in schools? Lucas, you're first."},{"speaker":"Lucas","text":"Yes, they should. Phones distract students. Moreover, they make bullying easier, because it continues after school. As a result, many students feel anxious all day."},{"speaker":"Moderator","text":"Hannah, your answer?"},{"speaker":"Hannah","text":"Admittedly, phones can be a distraction. Nevertheless, banning them is not the answer. On the contrary, schools should teach students how to use them responsibly."},{"speaker":"Lucas","text":"But that's an assumption. Where is the evidence that teaching works better?"},{"speaker":"Hannah","text":"Fair question. What I'm saying is that a ban doesn't teach anything. In other words, students will just use their phones more at home."}]},"question":"¿Qué le reprocha Lucas a Hannah?","options":["Que lo que dice es una suposición sin pruebas","Que habla demasiado","Que cambió de opinión","Que no respondió la pregunta"]},"answer":"Que lo que dice es una suposición sin pruebas","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Lucas dice: «But that’s an assumption. Where is the evidence that teaching works better?».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u10-l04-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l04","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u10-four-days","setting":"Unos colegas discuten la propuesta de trabajar cuatro días por semana.","speakers":[{"name":"Olivia","voice":"a"},{"name":"Ken","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"So, the four-day week. What worries me is the customers. Who answers the phone on Fridays?"},{"speaker":"Ken","text":"We'd take turns. The reason why other companies have done it is that people work better when they're rested."},{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"That may be true for some jobs. But we need to take into account that our clients expect us every day."},{"speaker":"Ken","text":"That's a valid point. So let's try it for three months and measure the results."},{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"OK, I find that convincing. All things considered, a trial is a good compromise."}]},"question":"¿Qué pide Olivia que se tenga en cuenta y cómo responde Ken?","options":["Que los clientes los esperan todos los días; Ken lo acepta y propone una prueba de tres meses","Que es caro; Ken lo niega","Que nadie quiere trabajar los viernes; Ken se enoja","Que es ilegal; Ken lo duda"]},"answer":"Que los clientes los esperan todos los días; Ken lo acepta y propone una prueba de tres meses","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Olivia: «we need to take into account that our clients expect us every day». Ken: «That’s a valid point. So let’s try it for three months».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u10-l04-e06","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l04","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lee y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u10-tips","document":"post","setting":"Consejos para escribir un buen argumento.","title":"Writing tips","lines":["How to write a convincing argument","Give reasons, not only opinions. \"I think it is bad\" is a point of view; \"it increases traffic by 30%\" is an argument.","Question your assumptions. If you assume that everyone agrees with you, your argument will be weak.","Take the other side into account. Mention the strongest counterargument and explain why your position is still valid.","Finish clearly. What readers remember is usually the last thing they read."]},"question":"Según los consejos, ¿qué diferencia hay entre un punto de vista y un argumento?","options":["Un argumento da una razón concreta, no sólo una opinión","No hay diferencia","El argumento es más corto","El punto de vista usa números"]},"answer":"Un argumento da una razón concreta, no sólo una opinión","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"El texto dice: «\"I think it is bad\" is a point of view; \"it increases traffic by 30%\" is an argument».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u10-l04-e07","lesson_id":"b2-u10-l04","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y elige lo que oyes","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Her argument was very convincing.","options":["Her argument was very convincing.","Her argument was not very convincing.","His argument was very convincing.","Her answer was very convincing."]},"answer":"Her argument was very convincing.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficult