ow","plot"]},"answer":"hardly","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-hardly"]},{"id":"b2-u11-final-e10","lesson_id":"b2-u11-final","position":10,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y elige lo que oyes","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"chapter","options":["chapter","no sooner","out of the blue","character"]},"answer":"chapter","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-chapter"]},{"id":"b2-u12-l01-e01","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l01","position":1,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Une cada palabra con su significado","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"dilemma","right":"dilema"},{"left":"weigh up","right":"sopesar / evaluar"},{"left":"pros and cons","right":"pros y contras"},{"left":"trade-off","right":"concesión / costo a cambio"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-dilemma","en-weigh-up","en-pros-and-cons","en-trade-off"]},{"id":"b2-u12-l01-e02","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l01","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"I am weighing ___ the pros and cons.","translation":"Estoy sopesando los pros y los contras.","options":["up","out","down","off"]},"answer":"up","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-weigh-up"]},{"id":"b2-u12-l01-e03","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l01","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"More money, less free time: that is the ___.","translation":"Más dinero, menos tiempo libre: ése es el costo.","options":["trade-off","dilemma","problem","decision"]},"answer":"trade-off","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-trade-off"]},{"id":"b2-u12-l01-e04","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l01","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u12-job-offer","setting":"Una amiga le cuenta a otra que tiene que decidir si se muda por trabajo.","speakers":[{"name":"Alice","voice":"a"},{"name":"Rosa","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Alice","text":"I've got a real dilemma. The Lisbon office has offered me a job as team manager."},{"speaker":"Rosa","text":"That's amazing! So why do you look worried?"},{"speaker":"Alice","text":"Because I'd have to move in a month. I've been weighing up the pros and cons all week."},{"speaker":"Rosa","text":"What does your gut feeling say?"},{"speaker":"Alice","text":"To go. But I'm having second thoughts because of my parents. They're getting older."},{"speaker":"Rosa","text":"Remember two years ago, when you turned down the job in Berlin? If you had taken it, you'd be speaking German by now."},{"speaker":"Alice","text":"I know. And if I were braver, I would have said yes immediately this time too."},{"speaker":"Rosa","text":"Every choice has a trade-off. But Lisbon is only a short flight away. You could visit them often."}]},"question":"¿Cuál es el dilema de Alice?","options":["Si aceptar un puesto en Lisboa y mudarse en un mes","Si cambiar de carrera","Si mudarse a Berlín","Si dejar su trabajo para cuidar a sus padres"]},"answer":"Si aceptar un puesto en Lisboa y mudarse en un mes","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Alice dice: «I’ve got a real dilemma. The Lisbon office has offered me a job as team manager… I’d have to move in a month».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u12-l01-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l01","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lee y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u12-guide","document":"post","setting":"Un artículo sobre cómo tomar decisiones importantes.","title":"How to make a big decision","lines":["Big decisions are hard because there is always a trade-off: more money but less free time, adventure but less security.","First, write down the pros and cons. Seeing them on paper helps you weigh them up more calmly.","Second, ask yourself what is really at stake. Will this matter in five years? If not, do not spend weeks on it.","Third, listen to your gut feeling. Research suggests that our first reaction often contains information we are not aware of.","Finally, accept that no decision is perfect. If we had a crystal ball, we would never make mistakes. We do not, so we learn from them."]},"question":"Según el artículo, ¿por qué son difíciles las grandes decisiones?","options":["Porque siempre se gana algo a cambio de perder otra cosa","Porque nunca hay información","Porque la gente es insegura","Porque llevan mucho tiempo"]},"answer":"Porque siempre se gana algo a cambio de perder otra cosa","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"El artículo dice: «there is always a trade-off: more money but less free time, adventure but less security».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u12-l01-e06","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l01","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lee y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u12-guide","document":"post","setting":"Un artículo sobre cómo tomar decisiones importantes.","title":"How to make a big decision","lines":["Big decisions are hard because there is always a trade-off: more money but less free time, adventure but less security.","First, write down the pros and cons. Seeing them on paper helps you weigh them up more calmly.","Second, ask yourself what is really at stake. Will this matter in five years? If not, do not spend weeks on it.","Third, listen to your gut feeling. Research suggests that our first reaction often contains information we are not aware of.","Finally, accept that no decision is perfect. If we had a crystal ball, we would never make mistakes. We do not, so we learn from them."]},"question":"¿Para qué sirve anotar los pros y los contras, según el artículo?","options":["Para sopesarlos con más calma","Para mostrárselos a otros","Para no tener que decidir","Para recordarlos años después"]},"answer":"Para sopesarlos con más calma","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"El artículo dice: «Seeing them on paper helps you weigh them up more calmly».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u12-l01-e07","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l01","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y elige lo que oyes","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"I've got a real dilemma.","options":["I've got a real dilemma.","I've got a real problem.","I haven't got a real dilemma.","We've got a real dilemma."]},"answer":"I've got a real dilemma.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-dilemma"]},{"id":"b2-u12-l01-e08","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l01","position":8,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Ordena las palabras","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["Write","down","the","pros","and","cons"],"translation":"Anota los pros y los contras."},"answer":"Write down the pros and cons.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["en-pros-and-cons"]},{"id":"b2-u12-l01-e09","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l01","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Responde en inglés","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"Have you decided about the new job? (no, todavía estás sopesando los pros y los contras)","translation":"¿Decidiste lo del trabajo nuevo?"},"answer":"No, I'm still weighing up the pros and cons.","accepted_answers":["No, I am still weighing up the pros and cons.","I'm still weighing up the pros and cons.","Not yet. I'm still weighing up the pros and cons."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-weigh-up","en-pros-and-cons"]},{"id":"b2-u12-l01-e10","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l01","position":10,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduce al inglés","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Tengo un verdadero dilema."},"answer":"I've got a real dilemma.","accepted_answers":["I have got a real dilemma.","I have a real dilemma.","I've got a big dilemma."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-dilemma"]},{"id":"b2-u12-l02-e01","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l02","position":1,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"If I had taken the job, I would ___ in Berlin now.","translation":"Si hubiera aceptado el trabajo, ahora estaría en Berlín.","options":["be","have been","been","being"]},"answer":"be","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Mixto: pasado distinto (had taken) → resultado presente (would be… now).","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-would-have"]},{"id":"b2-u12-l02-e02","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l02","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"If I ___ braver, I would have said yes.","translation":"Si fuera más valiente, habría dicho que sí.","options":["were","am","would be","will be"]},"answer":"were","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Mixto: presente distinto (if I were) → resultado pasado (would have said).","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-would-have"]},{"id":"b2-u12-l02-e03","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l02","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"I'm having second ___ about the trip.","translation":"Estoy dudando sobre el viaje.","options":["thoughts","ideas","minds","feelings"]},"answer":"thoughts","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-have-second-thoughts"]},{"id":"b2-u12-l02-e04","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l02","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u12-job-offer","setting":"Una amiga le cuenta a otra que tiene que decidir si se muda por trabajo.","speakers":[{"name":"Alice","voice":"a"},{"name":"Rosa","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Alice","text":"I've got a real dilemma. The Lisbon office has offered me a job as team manager."},{"speaker":"Rosa","text":"That's amazing! So why do you look worried?"},{"speaker":"Alice","text":"Because I'd have to move in a month. I've been weighing up the pros and cons all week."},{"speaker":"Rosa","text":"What does your gut feeling say?"},{"speaker":"Alice","text":"To go. But I'm having second thoughts because of my parents. They're getting older."},{"speaker":"Rosa","text":"Remember two years ago, when you turned down the job in Berlin? If you had taken it, you'd be speaking German by now."},{"speaker":"Alice","text":"I know. And if I were braver, I would have said yes immediately this time too."},{"speaker":"Rosa","text":"Every choice has a trade-off. But Lisbon is only a short flight away. You could visit them often."}]},"question":"¿Qué le recuerda Rosa a Alice?","options":["Que si hubiera aceptado el trabajo en Berlín, ahora hablaría alemán","Que en Berlín le fue mal","Que nunca le ofrecieron nada en Berlín","Que sus padres viven en Lisboa"]},"answer":"Que si hubiera aceptado el trabajo en Berlín, ahora hablaría alemán","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Rosa dice: «If you had taken it, you’d be speaking German by now» (pasado distinto → presente distinto).","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u12-l02-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l02","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u12-job-offer","setting":"Una amiga le cuenta a otra que tiene que decidir si se muda por trabajo.","speakers":[{"name":"Alice","voice":"a"},{"name":"Rosa","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Alice","text":"I've got a real dilemma. The Lisbon office has offered me a job as team manager."},{"speaker":"Rosa","text":"That's amazing! So why do you look worried?"},{"speaker":"Alice","text":"Because I'd have to move in a month. I've been weighing up the pros and cons all week."},{"speaker":"Rosa","text":"What does your gut feeling say?"},{"speaker":"Alice","text":"To go. But I'm having second thoughts because of my parents. They're getting older."},{"speaker":"Rosa","text":"Remember two years ago, when you turned down the job in Berlin? If you had taken it, you'd be speaking German by now."},{"speaker":"Alice","text":"I know. And if I were braver, I would have said yes immediately this time too."},{"speaker":"Rosa","text":"Every choice has a trade-off. But Lisbon is only a short flight away. You could visit them often."}]},"question":"¿Qué le dice su intuición a Alice y por qué duda?","options":["Que vaya, pero duda por sus padres, que están más grandes","Que se quede, porque no le gusta Lisboa","Que vaya, porque el sueldo es alto","No tiene ninguna intuición"]},"answer":"Que vaya, pero duda por sus padres, que están más grandes","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Alice dice: «To go. But I’m having second thoughts because of my parents. They’re getting older».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u12-l02-e06","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l02","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lee y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u12-guide","document":"post","setting":"Un artículo sobre cómo tomar decisiones importantes.","title":"How to make a big decision","lines":["Big decisions are hard because there is always a trade-off: more money but less free time, adventure but less security.","First, write down the pros and cons. Seeing them on paper helps you weigh them up more calmly.","Second, ask yourself what is really at stake. Will this matter in five years? If not, do not spend weeks on it.","Third, listen to your gut feeling. Research suggests that our first reaction often contains information we are not aware of.","Finally, accept that no decision is perfect. If we had a crystal ball, we would never make mistakes. We do not, so we learn from them."]},"question":"¿Qué dice el artículo sobre la intuición?","options":["Que la primera reacción suele tener información de la que no somos conscientes","Que no hay que hacerle caso","Que siempre acierta","Que es sólo para decisiones chicas"]},"answer":"Que la primera reacción suele tener información de la que no somos conscientes","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"El artículo dice: «our first reaction often contains information we are not aware of».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u12-l02-e07","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l02","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y elige lo que oyes","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"If I were braver, I would have said yes.","options":["If I were braver, I would have said yes.","If I were braver, I would say yes.","If I had been braver, I would have said yes.","If I were braver, I would have said no."]},"answer":"If I were braver, I would have said yes.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-would-have"]},{"id":"b2-u12-l02-e08","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l02","position":8,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Ordena las palabras","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["My","gut","feeling","says","I","should","go"],"translation":"Mi intuición me dice que tengo que ir."},"answer":"My gut feeling says I