común.","options":["ground","point","place","side"]},"answer":"ground","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-common-ground"]},{"id":"b2-u12-l03-e03","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l03","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"I don't want to take ___ in their argument.","translation":"No quiero tomar partido en su pelea.","options":["sides","part","place","care"]},"answer":"sides","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-take-sides"]},{"id":"b2-u12-l03-e04","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l03","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lee y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u12-neighbors","document":"notice","setting":"Un aviso de un servicio de mediación entre vecinos.","title":"Problems with your neighbors?","lines":["Community Mediation Service","Has a conflict with a neighbor gone on for too long? Noise, parking, trees, pets… We can help you resolve it.","Our mediators do not take sides. Their job is to help both people listen to each other and find common ground.","Not only is the service free, but it is also confidential. Under no circumstances will we share your information with the other person without your permission.","Should you need more information, please visit the community center from Monday to Friday."]},"question":"¿Qué hacen los mediadores, según el aviso?","options":["Ayudan a las dos personas a escucharse y encontrar puntos en común","Deciden quién tiene razón","Llaman a la policía","Cobran una multa"]},"answer":"Ayudan a las dos personas a escucharse y encontrar puntos en común","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"El aviso dice: «Our mediators do not take sides. Their job is to help both people listen to each other and find common ground».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u12-l03-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l03","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u12-team-conflict","setting":"Una reunión tensa de un equipo antes de presentar un proyecto.","speakers":[{"name":"Manager","voice":"a"},{"name":"Leo","voice":"b"},{"name":"Ines","voice":"a"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Manager","text":"I know there has been a conflict between design and sales. Let’s sort it out today."},{"speaker":"Leo","text":"The sales team wants to change the design again, two days before the launch. We can't keep doing that."},{"speaker":"Ines","text":"We're only asking because a big client is at stake. If we lose them, everyone loses."},{"speaker":"Leo","text":"I understand, but I have to stand up for my team. They've worked every weekend this month."},{"speaker":"Manager","text":"OK. Neither side has to back down completely. Ines, send one list of changes, the essential ones only. Leo, your team decides what is possible."},{"speaker":"Ines","text":"That sounds fair."},{"speaker":"Manager","text":"Good. Only then can we finish on time."}]},"question":"¿Cuál es el conflicto entre diseño y ventas?","options":["Ventas quiere cambiar el diseño dos días antes del lanzamiento","Diseño no quiere trabajar los fines de semana","Ventas perdió un cliente","Nadie quiere hacer el proyecto"]},"answer":"Ventas quiere cambiar el diseño dos días antes del lanzamiento","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Leo dice: «The sales team wants to change the design again, two days before the launch».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u12-l03-e06","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l03","position":6,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y elige lo que oyes","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"We can help you resolve the conflict.","options":["We can help you resolve the conflict.","We can help you avoid the conflict.","We can help them resolve the conflict.","We could help you resolve the conflict."]},"answer":"We can help you resolve the conflict.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-resolve","en-conflict"]},{"id":"b2-u12-l03-e07","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l03","position":7,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Ordena las palabras","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["A","mediator","helps","both","sides","listen","to","each","other"],"translation":"Un mediador ayuda a las dos partes a escucharse."},"answer":"A mediator helps both sides listen to each other.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["en-mediator"]},{"id":"b2-u12-l03-e08","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l03","position":8,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Responde en inglés","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"Who is right, your sister or your brother? (no quieres tomar partido)","translation":"¿Quién tiene razón, tu hermana o tu hermano?"},"answer":"I don't want to take sides.","accepted_answers":["I do not want to take sides.","I don't want to take sides!","Sorry, I don't want to take sides."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-take-sides"]},{"id":"b2-u12-l03-e09","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l03","position":9,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduce al inglés","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Trata de encontrar puntos en común."},"answer":"Try to find some common ground.","accepted_answers":["Try to find common ground.","Try and find some common ground."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-common-ground"]},{"id":"b2-u12-l04-e01","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l04","position":1,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Une cada palabra con su significado","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"stand up for","right":"defender (a alguien o algo)"},{"left":"back down","right":"ceder / echarse atrás"},{"left":"at stake","right":"en juego"},{"left":"common ground","right":"puntos en común"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-stand-up-for","en-back-down","en-at-stake","en-common-ground"]},{"id":"b2-u12-l04-e02","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l04","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"I have to stand up ___ my team.","translation":"Tengo que defender a mi equipo.","options":["for","to","with","on"]},"answer":"for","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-stand-up-for"]},{"id":"b2-u12-l04-e03","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l04","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Neither side wanted to back ___.","translation":"Ninguna de las dos partes quería ceder.","options":["down","up","out","off"]},"answer":"down","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-back-down"]},{"id":"b2-u12-l04-e04","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l04","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escucha y responde","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u12-team-conflict","setting":"Una reunión tensa de un equipo antes de presentar un proyecto.","speakers":[{"name":"Manager","voice":"a"},{"name":"Leo","voice":"b"},{"name":"Ines","voice":"a"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Manager","text":"I know there has been a conflict between design and sales. Let’s sort it out today."},{"speaker":"Leo","text":"The sales team wants to change the design again, two days before the launch. We can't keep doing that."},{"speaker":"Ines","text":"We're only asking because a big client is at stake. If we lose them, everyone lo